Source: rocket-hyperlinux-20260928/hyper-linux/src (read-only working copy).

Imported blocks (marked "imported from HL <file>" in the code):
- mm.c render_line(): /proc/<pid>/maps line layout (name column 73, newline escaped as \012) from
  proc_emulation.c proc_maps_fd(), adapted (8-digit address padding, trailing space after the inode,
  " (deleted)").

Everything else in src/mm is new code written for LKD. The VMA table design replaces HyperLinux's
guest_vma_t sorted array (guest.c guest_vma_replace/guest_vma_remove: linear memmove, 4144-byte entries)
with an AVL tree of ~100-byte entries.
